```

No behaviour change — just one less redundant `String()` call and a cleaner read. Same applies nowhere else; the other helpers already call their key-extractors once.
"}

{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: compute `done` once in `runCite`**

The pre-refactor closure evaluated `r.status === 'completed'` once and reused it for both `verdict` and `conclusion`. The split into `runVerdictOf`/`runConclusionOf` re-evaluates the same predicate twice:

```javascript
